{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013144-hellblazer-or-dr-strange-as-inspiration","id":1013144,"title":"Hellblazer or Dr. Strange as inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T07:17:28-08:00","id":1013144,"title":"Hellblazer or Dr. Strange as inspiration","content":"Which (if either, if not both) would you draw more inspiration from for your Mage chronicle: John Constantine or Dr. Stephen Strange?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:40:44-08:00","id":1013157,"title":"","content":"Dr. Strange has the more overall fantastic (in the literal sense) Mage 2nd / M20 feel. Hellblazer is more gritty and kind of fits the urban flair that the Revised edition wanted to establish - So it pretty much boils down to wanting to make the campaign &quot;Out There&quot;, or street-level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:47:13-08:00","id":1013198,"title":"","content":"Personally, i aim towards both.<br /> when under arete 5-6 they are pretty much hellblazer<br /> when they go over it, well.. it becomes Doctor Strange","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:23:50-08:00","id":1013320,"title":"","content":"I would look more towards Hellblazer in terms of inspiration.<br /> <br /> Constantine himself is actually a really interesting look at a skilled sorcerer operating in a world of mages and other supernaturals. The Hellblazer setting is where I go with on this more than the character himself. Hellblazer might seem a bit more &quot;Revised&quot; than not, but that's a lot of John's perspective at not being nearly as magically powerful as many of his contemporaries. This little corner of the DC universe is full of all of the supernatural stuff that the more gonzo side of Mage needs, and stays closer to the general themes and moods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:48:16-08:00","id":1013395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013144-hellblazer-or-dr-strange-as-inspiration?p=1013320#post1013320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would look more towards Hellblazer in terms of inspiration.<br /> <br /> Constantine himself is actually a really interesting look at a skilled sorcerer operating in a world of mages and other supernaturals. The Hellblazer setting is where I go with on this more than the character himself. Hellblazer might seem a bit more &quot;Revised&quot; than not, but that's a lot of John's perspective at not being nearly as magically powerful as many of his contemporaries. This little corner of the DC universe is full of all of the supernatural stuff that the more gonzo side of Mage needs, and stays closer to the general themes and moods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say something along this line. While I have not seen or read as much of either as I want to (slowly fixing that) I would say Hellblazer fits more with the idea of a Sorcerer or a Tremere while Mage cango the route of Dr. Strange. While this is not 100% always the case Constantine has spells and they work a certain way and make me feel they are Thaumaturgy Rituals in style. Now with Dr. Strange it gives me more of the Mage feel where you can do what ever you want as long as you have the building blocks of knowledge, so you can mix and match.<br /> <br /> But then again in my area Mage was never as popular and the few of us that did know the rules where that &quot;Mage group&quot; just because there was a purple book on the table. Yes I know it's weird but hey most people were playing V:tM or W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9486,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","user":"JBRocky","date":". 12-06-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:49:41-08:00","id":1013482,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that Constantine himself is actually not that great at magic by his universe's standards. A lot of the regulars he interacts with are way more powerful with magic than he is, or at least capable for far greater feats. What makes him special is how good he is at using his other skills to get around that. He's a master manipulator and crazy prepared (to the point where it's questionable who's better at preparing between him and Batman); though he can get in trouble if his reputation and wits aren't enough and he isn't prepared to take on someone more potent than him.<br /> <br /> Hellblazer also takes place in the same universe that has characters like Dr. Fate - and Dr. Strange is technically the knockoff of Dr. Fate - running around. The fact that there are people that are at least as scare of John as Dr. Fate says a lot about how clever John is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:46:51-08:00","id":1013649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013144-hellblazer-or-dr-strange-as-inspiration?p=1013482#post1013482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that Constantine himself is actually not that great at magic by his universe's standards. A lot of the regulars he interacts with are way more powerful with magic than he is, or at least capable for far greater feats. What makes him special is how good he is at using his other skills to get around that. He's a master manipulator and crazy prepared (to the point where it's questionable who's better at preparing between him and Batman); though he can get in trouble if his reputation and wits aren't enough and he isn't prepared to take on someone more potent than him.<br /> <br /> Hellblazer also takes place in the same universe that has characters like Dr. Fate - and Dr. Strange is technically the knockoff of Dr. Fate - running around. The fact that there are people that are at least as scare of John as Dr. Fate says a lot about how clever John is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good summary there.<br /> <br /> The other difference would be in style, as the two styles cater to vastly different level of grit and sheer magical shennenigans. Hellblazer is always going to be down in the gutters fighting against things usually losing something for every win he scrounges up. Dr. Strange and Dr. Fate will fight Gods and Magical Monster Invasions on a weekly basis and usually come out little worse for the wear. (The current Dr. Strange run by Aaron and Bacchalo seems to be going the other way, with some serious costs attached to Strange's victories)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}